          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"zuccoli-lamore-di-loredana-a4e4816a1fbe18c5\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":3,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.96,\"analysis\":\"Loredana’s written «ti amerò sempre» strongly presents her enduring love for Filippo as true. Its future form and farewell-note setting also give it substantial undertaking force: she pledges continuing love and attachment despite leaving him. Nothing indicates that the words are a reflex-like affective discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The future «amerò» can operate both as a prediction or avowal of enduring feeling and as a promise-like commitment; the surrounding «sarò tua» strengthens the latter without eliminating the former.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"written\",\"description\":\"A written declaration in the farewell lines Loredana has left for Filippo, subsequently recalled in narration.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Loredana is separating herself from Filippo as a self-sacrifice intended to save him and protect his ailing mother, not because her love has ended. The note reassures him that apparent distance will not alter her love or belonging to him. Her later explicit statement «Io amo Filippo» corroborates its sincerity, while the planned separation gives the future declaration a pledge-like relational force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"ev1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"«Non ti dimenticherò mai; ti amerò sempre; quanto più ti parrò lontana, tanto più sarò tua....»\",\"supports\":\"The categorical permanence marker «sempre» supports a strong truth-conditional avowal, while the future tense and «sarò tua» support an enduring relational undertaking.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"ev2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The narrator identifies these as «le poche righe che Loredana gli aveva lasciato» and says Filippo must already have read them.\",\"supports\":\"Establishes that the classified event is a deliberately composed written farewell message rather than a reflexive spoken outburst.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"ev3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Loredana later states: «Io amo Filippo, e mi sacrifico per lui.»\",\"supports\":\"Corroborates that the note presents a continuing loving state and belongs to her deliberate self-sacrificial separation from Filippo.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"ev4\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is annotated as affirmative future form, with exact match «ti amerò».\",\"supports\":\"Confirms the future morphology relevant to both enduring-state avowal and promise-like force.\",\"confidence\":0.99}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T and P naturally capture the written line as both an avowal of enduring love and a promise-like continuation of attachment. Its emotional and sacrificial context does not independently establish expressive/reflexive force, and no residual core function requires O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
